---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const root = "/temporal-research-agent";
const video = `${root}/demo/out/temporal-literature-review-demo.mp4`;
const poster = `${root}/deck-assets/worker-killed.png`;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Temporal lets us bring a research agent back to life"
  kicker="Temporal case study"
  intro="Improving the durability of our research pipeline using Temporal's Python SDK"
  description="A before-and-after rewrite of a literature-review agent as a durable Temporal Workflow, with code, recorded failure evidence, and implementation notes."
  image={poster}
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="tra stack">
    <nav class="tra__artifacts" aria-label="Project artifacts">
      <a href={`${root}/deck.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the deck <span>↗</span></a>
      <a href={`${root}/blog`}>Read the blog <span>→</span></a>
      <a href={`${root}/readme`}>Read the README <span>→</span></a>
      <a href="#code-comparison">Compare the code <span>↓</span></a>
    </nav>

    <figure class="tra__media">
      <video controls preload="metadata" poster={poster}>
        <source src={video} type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption>
        52 seconds. The Worker dies with two research Activities in flight;
        Temporal Web shows both retries and the completed Workflow.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="tra__premise prose">
      <h2>The original pipeline had already done useful work</h2>
      <p>
        A JavaScript workflow in the Code Intelligence Digest project sent ten
        research branches through SciX retrieval, deep dives, and podcast
        scripts, then produced two literature reviews. One client process held
        the schedule and inferred progress from files.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Python rewrite gives that progress to a Temporal Workflow. Network
        calls, heartbeats, clock reads, and artifact I/O run as Activities.
        Full evidence stays in an artifact store; Event History carries compact
        IDs, hashes, statuses, and paths.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="code-comparison" class="tra__section">
      <header class="tra__section-head">
        <p class="kicker">The code sample</p>
        <h2>The dependency graph stays recognizable</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="tra__code">
        <section>
          <h3>Before source</h3>
          <pre><code>phase('Research')
await pipeline(
  EPS,
  (it) =&gt; agent(/* prompt omitted */, &lbrace;
    label: 'research:' + it.s + '-ep' + it.ep,
    phase: 'Research',
  &rbrace;),
)

phase('Synthesis')
await parallel(literatureReviews)</code></pre>
          <p>Condensed for this page.</p>
          <a href={`${root}/before/phaseE_workflow.excerpt.js`}>Open the captured JavaScript excerpt</a>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>After source</h3>
          <pre><code>researched = await workflow.execute_activity(
    "research_angle",
    request,
    heartbeat_timeout=timedelta(seconds=30),
    retry_policy=self._retry_policy(review),
)</code></pre>
          <p class="cluster">
            <a href={`${root}/src/durable_research/workflow.py`}>Workflow</a>
            <a href={`${root}/src/durable_research/activities.py`}>Activities</a>
            <a href={`${root}/src/durable_research/worker.py`}>Worker</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tra__section tra__skill">
      <div class="tra__skill-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Beyond the demo</p>
        <h2>The Workflow became an agent skill</h2>
        <p>
          <code>run-durable-research</code> submits a Workflow and returns its
          identifiers. The calling agent can exit. Another agent on the same
          workstation can query progress or retrieve the cited report and
          provenance manifest later.
        </p>
        <p>
          Temporal owns branch state and retries. Activities own SciX, Code
          Intelligence Digest, artifact I/O, and future model calls.
        </p>
        <a href={`${root}/skills/run-durable-research/SKILL.md`}>Read the skill contract</a>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <img
          src={`${root}/deck-assets/workflow-completed.png`}
          alt="Recorded demo frame showing four completed research angles and the replacement Worker identity"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Four angles completed under the original Workflow run.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="tra__section">
      <header class="tra__section-head">
        <p class="kicker">Observed recovery</p>
        <h2>Event History records the handoff</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="tra__evidence">
        <figure>
          <img
            src={`${root}/deck-assets/worker-killed.png`}
            alt="Terminal showing the Worker killed while two Activities are in flight"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>The Workflow remains open after the Worker receives SIGKILL.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img
            src={`${root}/deck-assets/activity-attempt-two.png`}
            alt="Temporal Web showing two research Activities starting on attempt two"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>Events 7 and 10 show both research Activities on attempt two.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tra__section">
      <header class="tra__section-head">
        <p class="kicker">Assignment fit</p>
        <h2>Evidence for each evaluation criterion</h2>
      </header>
      <dl class="tra__criteria">
        <div>
          <dt>Technical depth</dt>
          <dd>
            A typed Python Workflow, four Activity types, a Worker, bounded
            concurrency, timeouts, heartbeats, retries, partial-result policy,
            compact history, and a durable external-request journal.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Clarity of explanation</dt>
          <dd>
            The deck puts the old and new code side by side. The blog and
            README trace the migration from process-local progress to recorded
            Workflow state.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Developer empathy</dt>
          <dd>
            The walkthrough names the crash windows, shows the Temporal Web
            evidence, explains trade-offs, and states which parts depend on
            local infrastructure.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Code quality</dt>
          <dd>
            Tests cover Workflow behavior, Activity boundaries, request
            journaling, artifact conflicts, caller exit, Worker replacement,
            recording invariants, and presentation contracts.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="tra__verification">
        <a href={`${root}/verification.md`}>Open the verification record</a>
        <span>·</span>
        <a href={`${root}/brief-alignment.md`}>Open the brief alignment</a>
        <span>·</span>
        <a href={`${root}/talk.md`}>Open the 12-minute talk plan</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="tra__boundary" aria-labelledby="runtime-boundary">
      <h2 id="runtime-boundary">Runtime boundary</h2>
      <p>
        The source, deck, documents, recording, and captured evidence are
        portable. Running the demo and live research integration is
        workstation-only. SciX and Code Intelligence Digest depend on local
        repositories, indexes, databases, services, and Worker configuration
        that are not included here. This page is the documentation package;
        the research service remains local.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </article>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .tra {
    --stack-gap: clamp(var(--space-xl), 8vw, var(--space-3xl));
    padding-block-end: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .tra__artifacts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__artifacts a {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 4.5rem;
    padding: var(--space-s);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    border-inline-end: var(--border-hairline);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .tra__artifacts a:last-child {
    border-inline-end: 0;
  }

  .tra__artifacts a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
  }

  .tra__media,
  .tra__evidence figure,
  .tra__skill figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra__media video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .tra__premise {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .tra__section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra__section-head {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .tra__section-head .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs);
  }

  .tra__section-head h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra__code {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra__code section {
    min-width: 0;
    padding-block-start: var(--space-s);
    border-top: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__code h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .tra__code pre {
    min-height: 15rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    padding: var(--space-m);
    overflow: auto;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .tra__skill {
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .tra__skill-copy {
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .tra__skill-copy > * + * {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-m);
  }

  .tra__skill img,
  .tra__evidence img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .tra__evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra__criteria {
    margin: 0;
    border-top: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__criteria div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 1fr) 3fr;
    gap: var(--space-l);
    padding-block: var(--space-m);
    border-bottom: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__criteria dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }

  .tra__criteria dd {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .tra__verification {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra__boundary {
    padding-block: var(--space-l);
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__boundary h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .tra__boundary p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .tra__artifacts,
    .tra__code,
    .tra__skill,
    .tra__evidence {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .tra__artifacts a {
      border-inline-end: 0;
      border-bottom: var(--border-hairline);
    }

    .tra__artifacts a:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .tra__criteria div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }
  }
</style>
